  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 295.01pt, "Abstract  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 325.25pt, "In Newtonian fluids, impact of a droplet on a liquid pool births a cavity, crown, capillary ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 346.01pt, "waves, and Worthington jet. The corresponding hydrodynamic events for elastic (or Boger) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 366.65pt, "fluids, however, remain an uncharted domain of comprehension and exploration. We ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 387.29pt, "thoroughly investigate, via experiments, theory, and simulations; how elastic energy storage, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 408.05pt, "fluid relaxation, and competitive inertio-elasto-capillarity govern the spatio-temporal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 428.71pt, "evolution of the cavity, the crown, and the ensuing Worthington jet in polymeric elastic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 449.83pt, "fluids. The events are systematically explored over a wide range of impact Weber (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.785pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(480.279pt, 449.932pt, "We")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(496.359pt, 449.932pt, " ) and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 470.95pt, "Deborah (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.807pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.088pt, 470.95pt, " De")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(143.9pt, 470.95pt, ") numbers, considering varied Newtonian and elastic fluid droplet-pool ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 491.83pt, "combinations; and revealing new, and distinct morphological regimes compared to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 512.47pt, "Newtonian counterparts. We illustrate that these new findings are purely driven by fluid-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 533.23pt, "elasticity, and not by viscosity or interfacial tension. We derive a theory for cavity radius ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 553.87pt, "evolution, using energy conservation within potential-flow framework. We show that ~30-40 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 574.51pt, "% of the droplet’s kinetic impact-energy may be stored as elastic energy by the stretching ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 595.3pt, "polymer chains during cavity expansion. Appealing to the FENE-P model, we derive a theory ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 615.94pt, "for the temporal evolution of the radius of the elongated Worthington jet. We show that in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 636.7pt, "elasto-capillary regime, competitive elastic- and capillary- stresses lead to exponential decay ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 657.34pt, "of the jet radius. The role of elastic stresses and the local velocity field in governing cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 678.1pt, "evolution, morphology, and jet formation are further elucidated through computer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 698.74pt, "simulations. Our findings significantly advance the uncharted paradigm of interplay between ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 719.5pt, "inertia, capillarity, and elasticity in droplet-pool interaction elasto-hydrodynamics.  ")
]

