#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.29pt, 790.08pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 84.98pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 111.14pt, "Hydrodynamic events consequent to the impact of a droplet on the free surface of deep, liquid ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 131.78pt, "pools have been extensively studied; albeit restricted to purely Newtonian fluid systems ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 152.54pt, "(droplet and pool liquids). Worthington pioneered in exploring the fluid dynamic events ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 173.18pt, "associated with the impact of a liquid droplet against a target body of liquid (Worthington ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 193.94pt, "1908), which subsequently attracted academic researchers down the century towards ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 214.58pt, "understanding the phenomena. Droplet impact on liquid surfaces may be commonly ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 235.22pt, "encountered in engineering systems, such as ink-jet printing, spray cooling, and spray ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 256.01pt, "painting and coating (Yarin 2006). Concurrently, uncontrolled and ballistic development of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 276.65pt, "such Worthington jets result in aerosol formation from ocean surfaces, soil erosion, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 297.41pt, "pesticide wastage and over-usage (Joung & Buie 2015; Nuruzzaman ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(403.75pt, 297.41pt, "et al. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.78pt, 297.41pt, "2016). ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 326.09pt, "Upon droplet impact on a deep liquid pool, the cavity formed expands freely to attain ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 346.85pt, "a maximum size, thereby displacing a substantial volume of liquid in the form of a rising ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 367.49pt, "crown. At higher impact velocity, the crown may disintegrate into a large number of tiny ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 388.25pt, "droplets. The cavity expansion is only temporary, as surface tension gradually counteracts, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 408.89pt, "and eventually arrests the downward motion of the liquid. Following this arrest, the flow ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 429.67pt, "reverses and the cavity undergoes collapse. The merging of capillary waves ejects a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 450.31pt, "Worthington jet from the cavity’s centre. This high-speed jet then undergoes Plateau-breakup, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 470.95pt, "resulting in the formation of one or more droplets travelling upwards (Castillo-Orozco ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.7pt, 470.95pt, "et al")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(520.42pt, 470.95pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 491.71pt, "2015). During cavity retraction, different sections of the cavity wall may merge, leading to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 512.35pt, "the entrapment of one, or more bubbles within the liquid (Oguz & Prosperetti 1990). At very ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 533.11pt, "high-velocity droplet impact, the rising cylindrical sheet at the upper edge of the crown bends ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 553.75pt, "inward as surface tension pulls on it, forming a canopy. This canopy then collapses towards ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 574.51pt, "the centre, generating a downward spiral jet that propagates towards the bottom of the cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 595.18pt, "(Wang ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.58pt, 595.18pt, "et al")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(127.58pt, 595.18pt, ". 2023).  ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 623.98pt, "Indeed, the hydrodynamics of the cavity depend on the impact parameters, i.e., impact ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 644.62pt, "velocity, force of gravity, droplet size, and physical properties such as viscosity, density, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 665.38pt, "surface tension. Depending on these parameters, various regimes viz.  floating, bouncing, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 686.02pt, "coalescence, and splashing may arise (Rein 1996). Our present research is focused on the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 706.66pt, "splashing regime. Research has been devoted to the splashing regime for Newtonian liquids, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 727.42pt, "especially towards the scaling of the maximum cavity size, the time to reach maximum cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 748.056pt, "depth (Engel 1966; Leng 2001), the spatio-temporal evolution of the cavity (Engel 1967; ")
]

