  #line-at(435.22pt, 165.74pt, "2019) on impact ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 186.38pt, "hydrodynamics have been studied. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 215.18pt, "After an exhaustive review of literature, it is evident that despite extensive research on ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 235.82pt, "Newtonian droplet-pool interactions through experimental, numerical, and analytical studies, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 256.61pt, "explorations and understanding the effect of rheology on the post-impact hydrodynamics of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 277.25pt, "droplet-pool interactions remains largely scarce, especially in the context of elastic liquids. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 298.01pt, "The presence of trace amounts of very long-chain polymers in a Newtonian solvent renders ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 318.65pt, "the resulting solution elastic (Boger fluids), which significantly influences the cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 339.29pt, "formation and collapse, crown dynamics, and jet ejection and disintegration processes, owing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 360.05pt, "to the drastically altered shear and extensional rheology. We often encounter ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 380.69pt, "viscoelastic/elastic fluids such as human mucus, paints, inks, gums, resins, medicinal gels, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 401.45pt, "microbial films, and industrial thickeners. The temporal evolution of viscoelastic/elastic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 422.11pt, "liquid filaments, and formation of daughter droplets has significance in systems ranging from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 442.87pt, "additive 3D printing, to arrest of droplet rebound on superhydrophobic surfaces (Dhar ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.46pt, 442.87pt, "et al.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 463.51pt, "2019; Kamaluddin ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(171.14pt, 463.51pt, "et al.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(198.65pt, 463.51pt, " 2024 & 2025), to the controlled deposition of cells in tissue ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 484.27pt, "engineering (Basaran ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(185.45pt, 484.27pt, "et al. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(220.73pt, 484.27pt, "2013). Understanding the fundamental mechanisms of the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 504.91pt, "fragmentation process influenced by viscoelastic/elastic effects may facilitate the control of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 525.67pt, "splashing and instabilities associated with droplet impact processes. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 554.35pt, "Experimental, theoretical, and computational studies have been reported in literature ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 574.99pt, "towards understanding the physical behavior underlying the thinning, and breakup of slender ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 595.78pt, "viscoelastic-liquid filaments (Clasen ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(252.41pt, 595.78pt, "et al. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(280.85pt, 595.78pt, "2006; Eggers & Villermaux 2008; Ardekani ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.7pt, 595.78pt, "et al. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 616.42pt, "2010; Turkoz ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(143.42pt, 616.42pt, "et al. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(174.14pt, 616.42pt, "2018; Bera ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(233.69pt, 616.42pt, "et al.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(259.61pt, 616.42pt, " 2026). A typical theoretical framework for studying ")
