  #line-at(492.34pt, 422.11pt, "1969), ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 442.87pt, "and liquid bridges stretched between two end-plates. In such systems, the flow conditions are ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 463.51pt, "externally controllable through either the imposed nozzle flow rate, or the stretching force ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 484.27pt, "applied to the endplates, enabling a relatively simplified description of the necking dynamics. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 504.91pt, "In these configurations, the position of the minimum neck diameter remains independent of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 525.67pt, "the axial coordinate, and the filament evolution is commonly analysed solely as a temporal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 546.31pt, "(0+1) problem within a Lagrangian framework.  ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 574.99pt, "In contrast, the dynamics of cavity formation, its growth, stall, and collapse, the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 595.78pt, "consequent Worthington jet-stretching, filament formation, and eventual breakup after impact ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 616.42pt, "of polymeric droplet on a deep polymeric pool remains very scarcely explored. Unlike ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 637.18pt, "conventional filament-thinning geometries, such a problem is intrinsically unsteady and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 657.82pt, "spatially evolving, arising from the collapse of capillary waves at the base of the formed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 678.58pt, "cavity. The emerging jet dynamics are governed by the impact velocity in conjunction with ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 699.22pt, "the propagation speed of the capillary waves along the cavity wall, where the latter is strongly ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 719.98pt, "influenced by polymer concentration and viscoelastic effects. Consequently, the minimum ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 740.62pt, "neck diameter is no longer confined to a fixed axial location; but instead, it evolves ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 761.4pt, "simultaneously in a coupled spatio-temporal (1+1) description of the necking and breakup ")
]

