// arXiv source page 13
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.05pt, 790.08pt, "13 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.92pt, "in the dynamics appear during both expansion and retraction phases. Since the viscosities of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.58pt, "the two liquids are same, and their surface tensions are very similar (see table 1), and all ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.34pt, "experimental conditions are identical, the observed changes in dynamics can be attributed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 144.98pt, "exclusively to elastic stress distribution and relaxation processes within the elastic liquid. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 173.78pt, "From the velocity contours (see figure 19), it is interpreted that polymer chain ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 194.42pt, "stretching along the cavity walls is non-uniform. The polymer chains undergo greater degree ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 215.18pt, "of stretching near the cavity base, than along the surrounding cavity wall, leading to a non-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 235.82pt, "uniform distribution of elastic stresses. This uneven stress distribution modifies, and delays ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 256.61pt, "the propagation of capillary waves along the cavity interface. During the onset of cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 277.25pt, "retraction phase, pressure builds up near the cavity base, tending to drive the cavity floor ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 298.01pt, "upwards. Simultaneously, the concentrated elastic stresses near the floor oppose this motion. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 318.65pt, "The resulting competition between the upward pressure force, and the resisting elastic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 339.29pt, "stresses leads to flattening of the cavity floor. Meanwhile, the capillary waves continue to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 360.05pt, "propagate towards the cavity’s centre. However, their smooth convergence is hindered by the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 380.69pt, "localized interplay between pressure and elastic stresses near the cavity floor, leading to the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 401.45pt, "formation of a notch-shaped profile. Consequently, the cavity develops a flattened bottom, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 422.11pt, "and inclined sidewalls, yielding trapezoidal cavity morphology than a hemispherical one in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 442.87pt, "the absence of elastic effects. The detailed discussions on the change in cavity shape will be ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 463.51pt, "in subsequent sections.  ")
]

