  #line-at(90.264pt, 148.46pt, "), the cavity exhibits a trapezoidal reversal, the maximum jet height is lowest among all ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 169.22pt, "other cases shown here, and the secondary droplet stays connected to a comparatively thicker ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 189.86pt, "filament. Since the elastic stresses within the jet do not relax, they continuously counteract ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 210.62pt, "the capillary stresses, thereby preventing droplet detachment. As the elasticity of both the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 231.26pt, "droplet and the pool is further increased (snapshots not shown for brevity), the maximum jet ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 252.02pt, "height decreases owing to the slower relaxation of elastic stresses, and the associated increase ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 272.69pt, "in elastic energy storage. As a result, jet development is delayed, a thicker filament is formed, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 293.45pt, "and pinch-off is completely suppressed. During cavity formation, polymer stretching stores ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 314.09pt, "elastic energy that relaxes only partially during cavity collapse. The resulting non-uniform ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 334.85pt, "elastic stresses resist radial inflow, particularly near the cavity base, causing the collapsing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 355.85pt, "cavity to transition from a hemispherical to a flatter, trapezoidal shape. With increasing ")
