  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(426.7pt, 454.27pt, "=0.026) to elucidate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 474.91pt, "the role of elastic stresses in the cavity and the jet dynamics. The simulations reveal the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 495.67pt, "elastic stress distribution within the jet and demonstrate how elasticity alters the velocity field ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 516.31pt, "relative to the pure water case. Figure 17 illustrates a qualitative and quantitative comparison ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 537.07pt, "of the predictions from our simulations with respect to our experimental observations. We ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 557.71pt, "portray here an array, at different time-stamps, and try to validate the computational model ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 578.35pt, "over a wide range of regimes observed during the droplet-pool interaction events. The ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 599.14pt, "simulations show excellent agreement with the experiments, over all the stages of cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 619.78pt, "formation and its collapse, and jet evolution. The cavity profiles, its depth and width, the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 640.54pt, "formation and morphology of the crown, the jet structure and height, and the satellite droplet ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 661.18pt, "dimensions at different time instants are compared in figure 17. The close morphological and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 681.94pt, "quantitative correspondence between the simulations and experimental results demonstrates ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 702.58pt, "the capability of the model to accurately capture the post-impact dynamics of elastic fluid ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 723.34pt, "droplet-pool interactions.  ")
]

