// arXiv source page 45
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.05pt, 790.08pt, "45 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.92pt, "Depending on the elasticity and the impact velocity, the liquid filament enters an elasto-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.58pt, "capillary regime in which the elastic stress balances the capillary stress, and filament radius ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.34pt, "decreases exponentially. Therefore, the observed elasto-capillary thinning of the Worthington ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 144.98pt, "jet may provide for a simple and effective approach for estimating the extensional relaxation ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.74pt, "time of elastic fluids directly from droplet-pool interaction studies.  ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 194.42pt, "Further, we observe that the cavity adopts a trapezoidal shape during reversal and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 215.18pt, "demonstrate that this shape evolution is driven purely by elasticity of the pool. A comparison ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 235.82pt, "of the cavity shape evolution in the water-glycerol and ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(363.67pt, 235.82pt, "De")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.59pt, 235.82pt, " = 0.05 cases with identical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 256.61pt, "viscosity shows that viscosity has a negligible effect on the formation of this shape. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 277.25pt, "Furthermore, as the elasticity of the liquid increases, the cavity size decreases because a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 298.01pt, "larger fraction of the kinetic energy of the cavity is converted into elastic energy via polymer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 318.65pt, "stretching. Through numerical simulations, we show the distribution of elastic stresses within ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 339.29pt, "the jet and find that polymers in the jet core undergo greater stretching than those near the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 360.05pt, "interface. As pinch-off approaches, the elastic stress increases sharply. Furthermore, for ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 380.69pt, "De")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.944pt, 380.69pt, "=0.026, polymer stretching converts the cavity's kinetic energy into elastic energy, thereby ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 401.45pt, "retarding the cavity expansion and causing the cavity to propagate at approximately half the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 422.11pt, "velocity observed in the pure water case. During cavity reversal, no vortex is observed inside ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 442.87pt, "the cavity in the elastic fluid, unlike in the pure water case, owing to the lower retraction ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 463.51pt, "velocity. Analysis of the local velocity field further reveals that the fluid velocity within the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 484.27pt, "jet is lower than that in the pure water case.The final morphology of the Worthington jet is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 504.91pt, "governed by the interplay between the growth rate of the Rayleigh instability and the inverse ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 525.67pt, "of the relaxation time. Depending on the elasticity of the droplet and the pool, this interplay ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 546.31pt, "leads to the formation of a very thin thread, a thin or thick filament, or a BOAS structure.  ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 574.99pt, "Our study provides new information and perspectives into the dynamics of elastic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 595.78pt, "fluid droplet impact on elastic fluid pools, a phenomenon relevant to several industrial ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 616.42pt, "applications; including spray coating, inkjet printing, manufacturing using resin and polymer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 637.18pt, "vats, and additive manufacturing, etc. Overall, we believe that our research significantly ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 657.82pt, "advances the fundamental understanding of the interplay between inertia, capillarity, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 678.58pt, "elasticity in controlling droplet-impact dynamics on complex fluids, and offers useful insights ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 699.22pt, "for applications involving elastic fluid free-surfaces and flows. ")
]

